1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,210
Integration, protecting ecosystems A.

2
00:00:06,210 --> 00:00:12,120
Daniel is reading an article about Jia Long Nature Reserve.

3
00:00:12,120 --> 00:00:16,830
Read with him and answer the questions below.

4
00:00:16,830 --> 00:00:25,140
Jia Long Nature Reserve is in Heilongjiang province in the north-east of China.

5
00:00:25,140 --> 00:00:29,040
It is one of the world's most important wetlands.

6
00:00:29,040 --> 00:00:34,100
The area provides food and cover for a lot of wildlife.

7
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:36,940
It is home to some rare birds.

8
00:00:36,940 --> 00:00:42,970
For example, about 20% of red-crowned cranes live in Jia Long.

9
00:00:42,970 --> 00:00:50,660
Many birds live in Jia Long all year round, while some go there only for a short stay.

10
00:00:50,660 --> 00:00:56,515
Most birds are active in the daytime, so you can easily watch them there.

11
00:00:56,515 --> 00:01:04,680
Some people want to make the wetlands smaller in order to have more space for farms and buildings.

12
00:01:04,680 --> 00:01:08,200
This will lead to less space for wildlife.

13
00:01:08,200 --> 00:01:15,360
Moreover, if fishermen keep fishing there, the birds will not have enough food to eat.

14
00:01:15,360 --> 00:01:21,400
Now the Chinese government has made laws to prevent all these things in Jia Long.
